==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|ge-|ġe-|lang=ang}} + {{term/t|ang|*rof||an array, number, host}} (attested only in compounds: {{term|secgrof|secgrōf|host of men|lang=ang}}, {{term|stæfrof|stæfrōf|alphabet|lang=ang}}). Cognate to modern Swedish {{term|greve||count|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/jeˈreːva/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=ġerēfa|m|ġerēfan}}

# a [[reeve]] or official with local jurisdiction under the king; the chief magistrate of a district

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-n-m|geref|alt1=ġerēf}}

====Descendants====
* English: {{l|en|reeve}}

